/// Regex prelude: loaded for definitions only, and only for a program that
/// writes regex syntax.
///
/// `system.text` declares the class a regex literal (`re"..."`) is built
/// through and a regex match pattern is tested with, found by its
/// `@regex_literal` and `@regex_match` methods. Loading it lets that syntax
/// work without a `use`, while naming `Regex` or `Match` still requires
/// `use system.text`. A program without regex syntax never loads it, so the
/// names it is written against, `Result` among them, stay free to declare.
use system.text
